# ~/.dotfiles/bat/config  (symlinked to ~/.config/bat/config)

# Auto day/night. `auto:system` reads the macOS system light/dark preference
# directly (reliable — plain `auto` relies on a terminal background-colour query
# that ghostty doesn't answer, so it fell back to Monokai). On Linux `auto:system`
# has no system pref to read and bat falls back to its terminal detection.
# Catppuccin Latte/Mocha ship built-in in bat 0.26.
--theme=auto:system
--theme-dark="Catppuccin Mocha"
--theme-light="Catppuccin Latte"
